    "https://tabor.edu/undergraduate/student-life/student-success/career-services/": {
      "title": "Career Services",
      "description": "Career Services | Tabor College JayShop CoreCampus Alumni Giving Apply Undergraduate Graduate Online Undergraduate Request Info Undergraduate Graduate Online Undergraduate Search for: Toggle navigation About Undergraduate Graduate & Online Athletics Performing Arts Video Viewbook Menu Apply Undergraduate Graduate Online Undergraduate Request Info Undergraduate Graduate Online Undergraduate Giving JayShop CoreCampus Alumni Athletics Performing Arts Search About Tabor Office of the President Board of Directors Mission, Vision, & Values History PR & Communications Faculty & Staff Employment Undergraduate Visit Campus Academic Programs Admissions Financial Aid Registrar Student Life Library Graduate & Online Graduate & Online Admissions Financial Aid Registrar Student Resources - Online Alumni & Friends Homecoming Connection Magazine Host Your Event Career Services Career Services Home » Undergraduate » Student Life » Student Success » Career Services Welcome to Tabor College’s Career Services! As a decidedly Christian college, we desire to help students find careers where they can use their God-given talents to glorify God.  Through collaboration with community partners, employers, alumni, and faculty, we offer Tabor students the opportunities to develop skills that will set them up for success in their chosen careers. We support student success by integrating vocational discernment, career readiness, and experiential learning in alignment with the college’s mission of preparing people for a life of learning, work, and service for Christ and His kingdom. The Career Services staff are here to help students: Develop cover letters and resumes Strengthen job-search skills Explore available job opportunities and internships Discuss graduate school application processes A complete résumé, cover letter & interview guide Looking for work on campus? Apply for on-campus positions ! Handshake Handshake is Tabor’s official job/internship portal , connecting students (and alumni) with employers in the area and across the globe. Handshake is a simple but powerful search tool to help students connect with employers. Over 1.5 million jobs and internships are posted annually from over 850,000 employers (9,000 in Kansas)—from every Fortune 500 company to nonprofits, startups, and more! Employers actively search for students with 250,000 searches for students per month. 80% of students with a COMPLETE profile receive a Direct Message from an employer. Student Login Employer Sign-Up Jobs & Internships (not through Handshake) Job Board Academic Programs Art & Design Biblical & Theological Studies Business Communication Computer Science Criminal Justice English Health & Physical Education History Music Nursing Science & Mathematics Social & Behavioral Science Teacher Education Admissions Affordability & Pricing Visit Campus Virtual Tour Admissions Checklist Admissions Deadline International Students Transfers Tuition & Expenses Accepted Student Info Meet Your Enrollment Team Frequently Asked Questions Request Info Apply Now Financial Aid Federal & State Aid Scholarships Net Price Calculator Fast Choice (Private Lending) Financial Aid Estimator Veterans/Dependents Benefits Visit Campus Preview Days Individual Campus Visit Early Registration Days Registrar Enrollment Confirmation Transcript Request - Undergraduate Course Schedules Acadeum Registrar Policies & Forms Commencement Senior Checklist Student Life Residence Life Student Organizations Spiritual Life Student Success Campus Recreation Center Student Government Ready for Class Checklist Move-In Student Resources Alumni Stories Connect with us Facebook Instagram Flickr YouTube YouTube (Live Events) Tabor College 400 South Jefferson Hillsboro, KS 67063 admissions@tabor.edu Phone: (620) 947-3121 Admissions Fax: (620) 947-6276 Tabor College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, or age in its programs and activities. Disclosures (incl