ms, as well as provide valid I.D. to the Human Resource Manager, located in the business office. Make sure you bring these I.D.s to campus! International students are required to apply for social security before being able to work. Contact Jim Paulus at jimp@tabor.edu for help applying. Faculty and Staff Downloads About Tabor Mission, Vision & Values History Theological Identity Tabor News Accreditation and Assessment Carson Center for Global Engagement Center for Mennonite Brethren Studies Map & Directions Office of the President Employment Faculty & Staff Connect with us Facebook Instagram Flickr YouTube YouTube (Live Events) Tabor College 400 South Jefferson Hillsboro, KS 67063 admissions@tabor.edu Phone: (620) 947-3121 Admissions Fax: (620) 947-6276 Tabor College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, or age in its programs and activities. Disclosures (including Title IX and Non-Discrimination) About Tabor Message from the President Mission, Vision & Values Employment Faculty & Staff Accreditation & Assessment Alumni & Friends Connect & Get Involved Homecoming Connection Magazine Host Your Event Alumni Contact Form Give Now Center for Mennonite Brethren Studies (CMBS) Academic Programs Undergraduate Graduate & Online Experience Tabor Athletics Performing Arts Tickets Student Life Visit Campus JayShop Carson Center for Global Engagement News & Events Events Calendar Tabor News Student Resources Financial Aid Library CoreCampus Canvas Registrar Request a Transcript Jobs & Internships COVID Locations Hillsboro Online Apply Now Undergraduate Graduate Online Undergraduate Request Info Undergraduate Graduate Online Undergraduate Give Back © 2026 Tabor College | Built by BitBrilliant"
